      "2": {
        "attributes": {
          "font-size": {
            "type": "number",
            "value": 19
          },
          "text": {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "OSC\n\nWire can both read and write OSC. This enables you to get OSC data into your patch. A common use case is to create a custom TouchOSC application on an Ipad or smartphone to control your patch, source or effect.\n\nWriting OSC enables you to get data out of your patch into other applications. Let's say you want to send the color of your shape to Ableton where it will modulate a filter. OSC Write is the node for you.\n\nTo get OSC into Wire simply use the OSC In node and connect it to the Read OSC node. Specify the address and you are off to the races.\n\nTo get  OSC out of wire use the Write OSC in conjunction with the OSC Out node.\n\nThe amount of parameters can be set in the inspector."
          }
        },
